{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012nEtAwdVLfDGBHXdBhBZ8V","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information from all the files. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Optimization Opportunities Analysis\n\nBased on my careful review of the hot path code in Shopify Liquid's parser and renderer, here are the key micro-optimization opportunities:\n\n### 1. **String Allocation in Variable#try_fast_parse** (variable.rb, lines 265-289)\n**Issue:** `filter_args << markup.byteslice(arg_start + 1, filter_pos - arg_start - 2)` creates unnecessary string allocations for quoted filter arguments. Every filtered variable parsing allocates new strings.\n**Opportunity:** Cache frequently used filter argument strings or use string interning for common values.\n\n### 2. **Redundant respond_to? Checks in VariableLookup#evaluate** (variable_lookup.rb, lines 175-178, 217-220)\n**Issue:** Multiple `respond_to?` calls per lookup:\n```ruby\n(object.respond_to?(:[]) && \n ((object.respond_to?(:key?) && object.key?(key)) ||\n  (object.respond_to?(:fetch) && key.is_a?(Integer))))\n```\nThis repeats for both single_lookup and full lookups path. Each lookup pays this cost multiple times.\n**Opportunity:** Combine respond_to? checks or use a single dispatch mechanism. Consider caching object type checks.\n\n### 3. **Repeated `instance_of?` Checks in Hot Loops** (condition.rb, context.rb, variable.rb)\n**Issue:** The render paths check `instance_of?(String)`, `instance_of?(Integer)`, `instance_of?(Float)`, `instance_of?(Array)` repeatedly:\n- variable.rb lines 514-518, 523-532\n- context.rb lines 116-121, 126-130, 147-152, 157-162, 279-283\n- condition.rb line 77-80\n\n**Opportunity:** Create a fast-path method `fast_to_s(obj)` or inline the type checks at the C level. Alternatively, use a single switch-on-type pattern.\n\n### 4. **Filter Invocation Dispatch Overhead** (strainer_template.rb)\n**Issue:** The `invoke_array` method (lines 90-106) uses a `case` on array length, but still falls through to splat for 4+ args:\n```ruby\nwhen 3 then send(method, input, args[0], args[1], args[2])\nelse send(method, input, *args)\n```\n**Opportunity:** Pre-cache the arity of filter methods during registration and avoid the case dispatch for known arities.\n\n### 5. **Context#lookup_and_evaluate Proc Check** (context.rb, lines 298-308)\n**Issue:** Every variable lookup checks `value.instance_of?(Proc)` and calls `respond_to?(:[]=)`. This is a second-order dispatch that delays simple lookups.\n**Opportunity:** Move Proc handling to a separate path or use a flag during context initialization to skip this check when no Procs are used.\n\n### 6. **Condition#interpret_condition Pattern Matching** (condition.rb, lines 182-211)\n**Issue:** Triple dispatch pattern: first check if `op.nil?`, then `case op`, then `respond_to?`:\n```ruby\nreturn context.evaluate(left) if op.nil?\nleft = Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value(context.evaluate(left))\n# ... then case/send\n```\n**Opportunity:** Use operator lambdas directly (already cached in @@operators) to avoid the final respond_to?/send call.\n\n### 7. **For Loop Variable Assignment** (tags/for.rb, lines 210-212)\n**Issue:** Each iteration does `context[var_name] = item` which likely goes through hash assignment with scope management. No fast-path for simple scope updates.\n**Opportunity:** Cache the scope reference or use a direct local var assignment path for hot loop variables.\n\n### 8. **Block#render_to_output_buffer Resource Limits Check** (block_body.rb, lines 258-278)\n**Issue:** Code duplicates the render loop twice (lines 259-268 vs 270-278) with/without `check_write`:\n```ruby\nif check_write\n  while (node = nodelist[idx])\n    # ... render loop\nelse\n  while (node = nodelist[idx])\n    # ... same render loop\n```\n**Opportunity:** Extract the loop body to eliminate duplication and improve CPU cache locality.\n\n### 9. **Expression#parse Number Parsing** (expression.rb, lines 70-159)\n**Issue:** `parse_number` uses sequential byte checks with multiple substring allocations:\n```ruby\nmarkup.byteslice(0, dot_pos).to_f  # line 143, 153\n```\n**Opportunity:** Use in-place float parsing via strtof-like approach or cache parsed numbers.\n\n### 10. **If Tag Block Evaluation** (tags/if.rb, lines 53-68)\n**Issue:** Linear search through blocks with `Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value()` call per block:\n```ruby\nresult = Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value(block.evaluate(context))\n```\n**Opportunity:** Short-circuit evaluation - if first block is true, skip to_liquid_value calls on remaining blocks.\n\n### 11. **Variable#render_to_output_buffer Filter Fast-Path Limitation** (variable.rb, lines 496-513)\n**Issue:** The single-filter fast-path only handles up to 2 args, then falls back to full render() which redoes work:\n```ruby\nelsif filters.length == 1 && context.global_filter.nil?\n  # ... only handles fa.empty? or fa.length == 1\n  else\n    render(context)  # REDOES all filters\n```\n**Opportunity:** Extend fast-path to handle 2+ arg filters inline without calling render().\n\n### 12. **VariableLookup#COMMAND_METHODS Check** (variable_lookup.rb, lines 162-164)\n**Issue:** Uses bitwise operations but still does `COMMAND_METHODS.include?(seg)` string lookups during initialization (lines 106, 123):\n```ruby\nif COMMAND_METHODS.include?(seg) ? 1 : 0\n```\nThis Array.include? call is O(n) in initialization.\n**Opportunity:** Use a Set or frozen hash instead of Array for COMMAND_METHODS.\n\n### 13. **String Scanning in block_body.rb** (lines 131-140)\n**Issue:** `blank_string?` byte-by-byte check is correct, but the same logic appears in Variable#simple_variable_markup (lines 23-27) - code duplication.\n**Opportunity:** Extract to a shared utility method or use a memoized constant.\n\n### 14. **Evaluation Dispatch in Variable#evaluate_filter_expressions** (variable.rb, lines 603-617)\n**Issue:** Creates temporary arrays and re-evaluates expressions. Could be optimized for common patterns.\n**Opportunity:** Lazy evaluation - evaluate filter args only when needed.\n\n---\n\n**Highest Impact Opportunities:**\n1. Cache/inline respond_to? checks in VariableLookup (used on every property access)\n2. Reduce instance_of? dispatch overhead in render paths\n3. Extend filter invocation fast-paths to 2+ args\n4. Eliminate loop duplication in BlockBody#render_to_output_buffer\n\nThese optimizations target the highest-frequency code paths in variable resolution, filter application, and block rendering."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e124f829-72f3-41c5-b2aa-159fc86e3514","uuid":"2b988cbe-63d0-474e-a8be-73559fcd44fa","timestamp":"2026-04-03T16:54:09.638Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm optimizing Shopify Liquid's parser and renderer for a performance benchmark. The current top score is 1.73. I need to find additional optimization opportunities in the hot paths.\n\nPlease read the following files carefully and identify potential micro-optimizations that could reduce allocations or speed up execution. Focus on:\n1. Frequently called methods that could be inlined or have fast-paths added\n2. Unnecessary object allocations (Array, String, Hash creation)\n3. Method dispatch overhead (respond_to?, send, etc.)\n4. Hot loops that could be optimized\n\nFiles to read:\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/variable.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/variable_lookup.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/context.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/block_body.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/strainer_template.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/standardfilters.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/expression.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/condition.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/tags/for.rb\n- /home/ubuntu/hive-swarm/shopify-liquid-task/silver-stallion/lib/liquid/tags/if.rb\n\nJust read the files and report back optimization ideas. Don't modify anything.","agentId":"aa2cb8b05fadf7e67","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information from all the files. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Optimization Opportunities Analysis\n\nBased on my careful review of the hot path code in Shopify Liquid's parser and renderer, here are the key micro-optimization opportunities:\n\n### 1. **String Allocation in Variable#try_fast_parse** (variable.rb, lines 265-289)\n**Issue:** `filter_args << markup.byteslice(arg_start + 1, filter_pos - arg_start - 2)` creates unnecessary string allocations for quoted filter arguments. Every filtered variable parsing allocates new strings.\n**Opportunity:** Cache frequently used filter argument strings or use string interning for common values.\n\n### 2. **Redundant respond_to? Checks in VariableLookup#evaluate** (variable_lookup.rb, lines 175-178, 217-220)\n**Issue:** Multiple `respond_to?` calls per lookup:\n```ruby\n(object.respond_to?(:[]) && \n ((object.respond_to?(:key?) && object.key?(key)) ||\n  (object.respond_to?(:fetch) && key.is_a?(Integer))))\n```\nThis repeats for both single_lookup and full lookups path. Each lookup pays this cost multiple times.\n**Opportunity:** Combine respond_to? checks or use a single dispatch mechanism. Consider caching object type checks.\n\n### 3. **Repeated `instance_of?` Checks in Hot Loops** (condition.rb, context.rb, variable.rb)\n**Issue:** The render paths check `instance_of?(String)`, `instance_of?(Integer)`, `instance_of?(Float)`, `instance_of?(Array)` repeatedly:\n- variable.rb lines 514-518, 523-532\n- context.rb lines 116-121, 126-130, 147-152, 157-162, 279-283\n- condition.rb line 77-80\n\n**Opportunity:** Create a fast-path method `fast_to_s(obj)` or inline the type checks at the C level. Alternatively, use a single switch-on-type pattern.\n\n### 4. **Filter Invocation Dispatch Overhead** (strainer_template.rb)\n**Issue:** The `invoke_array` method (lines 90-106) uses a `case` on array length, but still falls through to splat for 4+ args:\n```ruby\nwhen 3 then send(method, input, args[0], args[1], args[2])\nelse send(method, input, *args)\n```\n**Opportunity:** Pre-cache the arity of filter methods during registration and avoid the case dispatch for known arities.\n\n### 5. **Context#lookup_and_evaluate Proc Check** (context.rb, lines 298-308)\n**Issue:** Every variable lookup checks `value.instance_of?(Proc)` and calls `respond_to?(:[]=)`. This is a second-order dispatch that delays simple lookups.\n**Opportunity:** Move Proc handling to a separate path or use a flag during context initialization to skip this check when no Procs are used.\n\n### 6. **Condition#interpret_condition Pattern Matching** (condition.rb, lines 182-211)\n**Issue:** Triple dispatch pattern: first check if `op.nil?`, then `case op`, then `respond_to?`:\n```ruby\nreturn context.evaluate(left) if op.nil?\nleft = Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value(context.evaluate(left))\n# ... then case/send\n```\n**Opportunity:** Use operator lambdas directly (already cached in @@operators) to avoid the final respond_to?/send call.\n\n### 7. **For Loop Variable Assignment** (tags/for.rb, lines 210-212)\n**Issue:** Each iteration does `context[var_name] = item` which likely goes through hash assignment with scope management. No fast-path for simple scope updates.\n**Opportunity:** Cache the scope reference or use a direct local var assignment path for hot loop variables.\n\n### 8. **Block#render_to_output_buffer Resource Limits Check** (block_body.rb, lines 258-278)\n**Issue:** Code duplicates the render loop twice (lines 259-268 vs 270-278) with/without `check_write`:\n```ruby\nif check_write\n  while (node = nodelist[idx])\n    # ... render loop\nelse\n  while (node = nodelist[idx])\n    # ... same render loop\n```\n**Opportunity:** Extract the loop body to eliminate duplication and improve CPU cache locality.\n\n### 9. **Expression#parse Number Parsing** (expression.rb, lines 70-159)\n**Issue:** `parse_number` uses sequential byte checks with multiple substring allocations:\n```ruby\nmarkup.byteslice(0, dot_pos).to_f  # line 143, 153\n```\n**Opportunity:** Use in-place float parsing via strtof-like approach or cache parsed numbers.\n\n### 10. **If Tag Block Evaluation** (tags/if.rb, lines 53-68)\n**Issue:** Linear search through blocks with `Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value()` call per block:\n```ruby\nresult = Liquid::Utils.to_liquid_value(block.evaluate(context))\n```\n**Opportunity:** Short-circuit evaluation - if first block is true, skip to_liquid_value calls on remaining blocks.\n\n### 11. **Variable#render_to_output_buffer Filter Fast-Path Limitation** (variable.rb, lines 496-513)\n**Issue:** The single-filter fast-path only handles up to 2 args, then falls back to full render() which redoes work:\n```ruby\nelsif filters.length == 1 && context.global_filter.nil?\n  # ... only handles fa.empty? or fa.length == 1\n  else\n    render(context)  # REDOES all filters\n```\n**Opportunity:** Extend fast-path to handle 2+ arg filters inline without calling render().\n\n### 12. **VariableLookup#COMMAND_METHODS Check** (variable_lookup.rb, lines 162-164)\n**Issue:** Uses bitwise operations but still does `COMMAND_METHODS.include?(seg)` string lookups during initialization (lines 106, 123):\n```ruby\nif COMMAND_METHODS.include?(seg) ? 1 : 0\n```\nThis Array.include? call is O(n) in initialization.\n**Opportunity:** Use a Set or frozen hash instead of Array for COMMAND_METHODS.\n\n### 13. **String Scanning in block_body.rb** (lines 131-140)\n**Issue:** `blank_string?` byte-by-byte check is correct, but the same logic appears in Variable#simple_variable_markup (lines 23-27) - code duplication.\n**Opportunity:** Extract to a shared utility method or use a memoized constant.\n\n### 14. **Evaluation Dispatch in Variable#evaluate_filter_expressions** (variable.rb, lines 603-617)\n**Issue:** Creates temporary arrays and re-evaluates expressions. Could be optimized for common patterns.\n**Opportunity:** Lazy evaluation - evaluate filter args only when needed.\n\n---\n\n**Highest Impact Opportunities:**\n1. Cache/inline respond_to? checks in VariableLookup (used on every property access)\n2. Reduce instance_of? dispatch overhead in render paths\n3. Extend filter invocation fast-paths to 2+ args\n4. Eliminate loop duplication in BlockBody#render_to_output_buffer\n\nThese optimizations target the highest-frequency code paths in variable resolution, filter application, and block rendering."}],"totalDurationMs":26098,"totalTokens":52621,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3896,"cache_read_input_tokens":46914,"output_tokens":1806,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3896},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
